#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1361 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "FLIPPED violation -> skipped by the top-level-or board's R-5.25 split (wave 1 group D, 2026-09-12, PLAN-top-level-or-split \u00a74): the split left this parent a bare empty(ARMCD) leaf, so both halves were pinned Requirements.Variables.All [ARMCD, ARM] and the absent-ARMCD dataset is now SKIPPED naming the variable. The ruling and its argument are in documentation/derivation/absent-column-verdicts.tsv (verdict 2-2: the pair-consistency question is unanswerable without both columns; ARM/ARMCD are Expected in DM, so the absence is separately reported). This is a RULED change, not a silently injected guard - the flood this fixture used to assert was executed deliberately by Fix #331 and retired deliberately here. History: before Fix #330 the machine-emitted var_exists guard kept this dataset silent; Fix #331 flipped it to violation (absent = all-missing, empty(X) TRUE on every row); the R-5.25 split re-ruled it to skipped. If this fixture ever reports a VIOLATION again, the gate has been removed - escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | Treatment A
